{
  "title": "Scheduler — Overview",
  "uid": "scheduler-overview",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "timezone": "browser",
  "time": { "from": "now-1h", "to": "now" },
  "refresh": "10s",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Service up",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [{ "expr": "up{job=\"scheduler-api\"}", "refId": "A" }]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Process CPU (rate)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 9, "x": 6, "y": 0 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        { "expr": "rate(process_cpu_seconds_total{job=\"scheduler-api\"}[5m])", "refId": "A" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Heap used (bytes)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 9, "x": 15, "y": 0 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        { "expr": "nodejs_heap_size_used_bytes{job=\"scheduler-api\"}", "refId": "A" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Event loop lag (p99, seconds)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 9, "x": 6, "y": 8 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "nodejs_eventloop_lag_p99_seconds{job=\"scheduler-api\"}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Booking attempts by outcome (rate/5m)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 9, "x": 15, "y": 8 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "description": "outcome=\"booked\" is a success. no_free_* is the application-level check refusing a full window. *_taken_concurrently is ADR-0002's exclusion constraint catching a race the application check missed — a nonzero rate there is the guarantee visibly working, not an error budget being spent.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(scheduler_api_booking_attempt_total{job=\"scheduler-api\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Availability check latency (p95, seconds)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 9, "x": 6, "y": 16 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(scheduler_api_availability_check_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"scheduler-api\"}[5m])))",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Deferred — idempotency replay rate",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 9, "x": 15, "y": 16 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Not built yet.** `IdempotencyInterceptor` has no counter of its own (claim vs. replay vs. conflict) — see `docs/09_devops_infrastructure.md`. Trigger: idempotency behaviour becomes a debugging question in practice, not just a correctness property. Add the counter in `infrastructure/http/idempotency/`, then a panel here."
      }
    }
  ]
}
